            <div xml:id="d952">

                <pb facs="0994" n="874" sameAs="frus:frus1931v02/pg874"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">817.00 Johnson Electoral Mission/195:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        Nicaragua</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Hanna</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-05-11T18:00:00-04:00">May 11, 1931—6
                    p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>115. Has President Moncada designated Major Price yet as <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >suplente</hi> to the Chairman of the Electoral Commission? He must make his
                    definite plans very shortly and desires to know what to expect in this
                    connection.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
